# Surjectivity of the Kummer correspondence onto degree-`p` Galois extensions

For a field `k` containing a primitive `p`-th root of unity `ζ` (`p` prime), every
Galois subextension `L/k` inside a fixed ambient field `K'` of degree `p` is a
Kummer extension `k(a^{1/p})` for some class `a ∈ kˣ/(kˣ)^p`.  This is the
surjectivity half of the classical Kummer-theoretic description of the degree-`p`
Galois extensions of `k`.

The mathematical content is bundled into Mathlib's `isCyclic_tfae`
(`Mathlib.FieldTheory.KummerExtension`): a cyclic extension of degree `p` over a
field containing a primitive `p`-th root of unity is generated by a `p`-th root
`α` of an element of `k`.  The rest of the file checks that the Kummer field of
the class of `α ^ p` is exactly `L`.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.NK.LocalAnabelian.Kummer.Quot
